# L §2.4 Canonical format: "Header first: model, then tally, on, start, end, use lines (by name), same lines (by left
# side), notes"; "Sections in this kind order: source, unit, kind, axis, index, place, input, band, def, fill, move,
# regime, ask, version"; "Within a kind, sections are sorted by id (ASCII); kinds are printed parents before
# subkinds" (alpha waits for its parent zeta; beta and zeta by id); "Versions come last, sorted by known date (a window
# by its first day), then id" (v1's window starts 2026-01-01; a3 and v2 share 2026-03-01, so by id); "One blank line
# between sections, always, one-line sections included". ASCII puts PLN before hour. E §3.1 step 1: the reality's
# hash is the sha256 of the canonical text (its value is refcore's, so matched by prefix). tally 2.1.6 (issue
# #74): reprint pins a joint model's members as run does, so the members a.tally and b.tally are given,
# with their hashes.
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use b = "b.tally" sha256 "3558bfc60c0cc70d33354bb1c25ed55c8ff26980aa36ff2be6096b8e53562746"
  use a = "a.tally" sha256 "2ebb0757232e7a6b22996db04a17cfaa41ae24c2936a9c4a3dafc32d9a9a4cac"
  same b.x = a.x
  same a.y = b.y
  note "n"
version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-01
  x = 2
version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known window(2026-01-01, 2026-06-30)
  replace x = 3


version a3
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-01
  replace x = 4
ask q: x
kind zeta: assets
kind beta
kind alpha: zeta
input x: int
source s "src"
unit hour "h"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
=== a.tally
model a
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

input x: int

input y: int
=== b.tally
model b
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

input x: int

input y: int
